  "findings": [
    "Both candidates retain large direction-dependent output differences with the ground-connected 500-ohm load at both step sizes and complementary-input choices.",
    "Changing load connection changes branch selection; the supply-loaded sink-RE10 tied-input sweep appears direction-independent at 1 mV steps but exposes a branch difference at 0.5 mV. Coarse agreement alone is insufficient.",
    "The published LS00 curve provides an independent transition-region reference. Its unspecified fixture details and absence of forward/reverse bounds do not justify exact fitting or a physical-hysteresis conclusion.",
    "Review of the TI 1985 LS00 drawing found no supported topology correction; candidate changes require independent device evidence rather than removing a depicted feedback diode to force oscillation."
  ],
